Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project bundles / depends on the following open-source components. Their
licenses are reproduced by their respective packages under node_modules.

- React, React DOM .................................. MIT
- Vite, @vitejs/plugin-react ....................... MIT
- CodeMirror 6 (@codemirror/*), @uiw/react-codemirror  MIT
- @lezer/* ......................................... MIT
- Zustand .......................................... MIT
- TypeScript ....................................... Apache-2.0
- Vitest, jsdom, ESLint, Prettier .................. MIT

Runtime (loaded at run time, not bundled in source):

- Pyodide (CPython compiled to WebAssembly) ........ MPL-2.0
  https://github.com/pyodide/pyodide
  Loaded from a pinned CDN path at run time. Pyodide's MPL-2.0 applies at the
  file level to Pyodide's own files; it does not affect Codelapse's source.

Note: no GPL-licensed component is distributed with the browser tier. When the
server tier ships, native debuggers such as GDB (GPLv3) are used only as a
separate process on the server and are never linked into or distributed with
the client bundle.
